const idSchema = z.coerce.number().int().positive();

app.get('/users/:id', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  const parsed = idSchema.safeParse(req.params.id);
  if (!parsed.success) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid id' });
  // ...lookup with parameterized query, never string concatenation
});
```

For any future DB code: use parameterized queries (`pg`'s `$1` placeholders, Prisma, Knex bindings) — never template strings.

---

### 6. No structured logging or error handling (A09: Security Logging & Monitoring Failures)

**Issue:** Only `console.log` on startup. No request logging, no error middleware. Unhandled errors will produce default Express stack traces (info disclosure) and won't be auditable.

**Severity:** Medium

